<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Bank plans unchanged 1.80 dmk dividend.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank plans unchanged 1.80 dmk dividend.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG said on Tuesday its management planned to propose an unchanged dividend of 1.80 marks per five-mark share for 1996.</p>
<p>The bank announced the dividend proposal in a brief statement. Its supervisory board meets today.</p>
<p>The dividend is in line with analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
